
# Contributor Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in this project a welcoming and harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of background, identity, experience, or personal circumstances.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

- Demonstrating empathy and kindness.
- Respecting different viewpoints and experiences.
- Giving and accepting constructive feedback.
- Taking responsibility for mistakes.
- Focusing on what is best for the community.

Unacceptable behavior includes:

- Harassment, insults, or discriminatory comments.
- Personal or political attacks.
- Publishing private information without permission.
- Any conduct that creates an unsafe environment.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing acceptable behavior. They may remove or reject contributions and comments that violate this Code of Conduct.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces, including repository discussions, issues, pull requests, and other interactions involving the project.

## Enforcement

Instances of abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behavior may be reported privately to the project maintainer through an appropriate GitHub contact channel.

All complaints will be reviewed fairly and confidentially, with appropriate action taken when necessary.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Maintainers will consider the following guidelines when determining consequences.

### 1. Correction

Minor inappropriate behavior may result in a private warning and an explanation of the violation.

### 2. Warning

A more serious or repeated violation may result in a formal warning and restrictions on participation.

### 3. Temporary Ban

Serious violations may result in temporary suspension from project interactions.

### 4. Permanent Ban

Repeated harassment or severe misconduct may result in permanent exclusion from the project.

